## Submission class

- [ ] Research artifact or independent audit; no canonical promotion requested
- [ ] Canonical theorem promotion requested
- [ ] Repository process, documentation, or tooling

An ordinary merge does not promote a mathematical claim. For required items that do
not apply, write `none` or `not applicable`.

## Base and state

- Base branch:
- Exact base commit:
- Theorem `state_version` at that base:
- PR head commit reviewed:
- Target route or repository area:

## Exact question or change

State the precise research question, theorem, correction, or behavior changed. If this
is mathematical, state all objects and hypotheses and distinguish finite, local,
arbitrary-packing, scaffold, and global-minimizer conclusions.

## Dependencies and predecessors

List canonical theorem IDs, source paths, and any noncanonical assumptions used. Link
the closest predecessor reports, issues, discussions, and open PRs. Explain what this
submission adds or independently checks.

## Evidence and verification

Describe the proof or implementation evidence. Include exact reproduction commands,
inputs, arithmetic or environment requirements, tests, and results. Identify which
parts were checked independently and by whom. State what the checks establish and what
they do not establish.

## Limitations and status

- Remaining proof obligations or known limitations:
- Exact lifecycle classification requested (unreviewed, audited-working, conditional,
  regression, superseded, rejected, or canonical promotion):
- Cross-PR or cross-branch dependencies:
- Canonical theorem delta: zero unless a reviewed promotion is explicitly requested:

## Promotion transaction (only if requested)

- [ ] Complete proof and audit are included; this is not a report-only promotion.
- [ ] `state_version`, `docs/STATE.md`, target route/frontier, and active prompt are
      updated as needed in this same PR.
- [ ] Dependency edges and load-bearing certificate registrations are updated.
- [ ] Generated theorem metadata and views were regenerated through their generators.
- [ ] One independent AI-agent mathematical audit is linked, combining full proof
      reconstruction and adversarial bridge/regression testing. It records the
      exact reviewed commit, reviewing agent/model when known, inputs, commands,
      verdict and unresolved points. No human mathematical review is required.
- [ ] `python3 tools/check_theorem_state.py` and the relevant certificates pass.

## Attribution and AI assistance

- Contributors and predecessor work to credit:
- AI tools/models used, when known, and their role (proof drafting, code, search,
  verification, or none):
- Source, license, or citation notes:

## Modified files

List every created, modified, or deleted file and why it belongs in this PR.

## Outstanding limitations and owner decisions

List unresolved blockers, follow-up work, and any owner decision needed. State explicitly
what was not verified. Do not claim external peer review unless it occurred.
